OL,3,W"###"###"###T//,.-,.,,.-.-,.,/,-./,-,./
OL,4,CThe footballer who was the world's     
OL,5,Cfirst cross-border signing             
OL,6,GIt might seen unthinkable in today's   
OL,7,Gera of huge wages and multi-million    
OL,8,Gpound transfer fees, but the early     
OL,9,Gdays of football were strictly an      
OL,10,Gamateur affair.                        
OL,12,FThere was fierce debate throughout the 
OL,13,F1870s and 1880s regarding payment of   
OL,14,Fplayers, as clubs increasingly sought  
OL,15,Fto secure the best talent.             
OL,17,FAt the forefront of this were a number 
OL,18,Fof Scots. Among them was James 'Jimmy' 
OL,19,FLang, a former shipyard worker         
OL,20,Fconsidered by some historians to be    
OL,21,Fthe world's first migrant professional 
OL,22,Ffootball player.                  G4/4 
OL,23,D]CNews IndexG102CFlashG150CRegionalG160
